INT. TAXIDERMY MUSEUM - BACK GALLERY - NIGHT

Glass cases. A stuffed polar bear mid-roar. Six figures in dark clothes crouch behind a display of Arctic foxes.

CASSIUS BELL (50s, mastermind, reading glasses on a chain) taps a tablet. WREN ODUYA (20s, climber, harness). LAZARO PRIETO (30s, safecracker, toolroll). MAI LINH TRAN (30s, hacker, headset). DOROTHEA "DOT" KESSLER (60s, retired guard, inside woman). RUFUS ALDER (40s, muscle, silent).

CASSIUS
Camera eleven loops in ten seconds.

MAI LINH
Eight. Eight, Cassius, I said eight.

DOT
He walks the corridor at twelve forty. Always.

LAZARO
It's twelve thirty-eight.

WREN
Rope is set. I go on your mark.

CASSIUS
Wait for--

DOT
Footsteps.

Everyone freezes. Rufus raises one huge hand, palm flat.

MAI LINH
That's not him, that's the heating.

DOT
It's him.

LAZARO
It's the heating!

WREN
Tell me which, I'm hanging out here!

CASSIUS
Dot. Which?

DOT
(whispering)
Twelve forty. It's him.

A flashlight beam sweeps across the foxes. Rufus slowly, silently, pulls the bear's display curtain across them all. Darkness.

The footsteps stop. A long beat. Then a cough, and they move on.

MAI LINH
(exhaling)
Looping now.

CASSIUS
Wren, go.
